<title>THAILAND: Thai Farmers Bank mandates $125 loan.</title>
<headline>Thai Farmers Bank mandates $125 loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Farmers Bank Plc, Thailand's third largest commercial bank, has authorised ABN AMRO NV to manage a $125 million five-year loan, a bank executive told Reuters.</p>
<p>The executive said the loan carried an interest rate at 27 basis points above Libor.</p>
</text>
